# ACCESS BLOCKING — not rule injection.
#
# `.cursorignore` hides files from Agent, Tab, Inline Edit, and @ mentions.
# It does NOT decide which Project Rules load into the model context.
#
# Path-scoped rules (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc` with `globs:`) INCLUDE instructions
# when a matching file is already in context. That is a different mechanism.
# Docs: https://cursor.com/docs/reference/ignore-file
#
# This folder exists so you can prove the contrast in HOW-TO-VALIDATE.md:
# `@local/private-notes.md` should be blocked; `apps/api` files should still
# be readable, and API rules should still attach when those files are in play.

local/
